  "id": "brightness-perception",
  "term": "brightness perception",
  "definition": "Brightness perception is the experience of how dark or bright something looks, corresponding to its luminance. The packet also indicates that this perceived brightness can change with how a scene or object is organized in depth, even when the retinal image stays the same.",
